        "content": "<p>These two imports work separately, but fail when in the same file:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.«».</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Presumably <code>Lean.«».Meta.Basic</code> resolves to <code>Lean//Meta/Basic.olean</code> which is aliased by the filesystem to  the other name, but ends up registered as a different module</p>",
        "id": 582232762,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1774633605
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.«..».</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>also shows the same behavior</p>",
        "id": 582232823,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1774633628
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Probably a less cursed example involves one module being symlinked to another, where again Lean's environment merger is not made aware that the modules are identical.</p>",
